4. API Endpoints
4.1 Public find and connect (no auth)
    • GET /api/services – List available services
    • GET /api/services/nearby?lat=&lng= – Services plus nearby available-worker counts (for Get Started tiles)
    • GET /api/workers/nearby?service_id=&lat=&lng= – Nearby verified, available workers (phone hidden)
    • POST /api/book – Connect with name + phone (guest) or an auth token (optional account)
        Body: name, phone, service_id, latitude, longitude, optional worker_id
        Response includes the worker phone only after the booking is created
    • POST /api/contact – Contact form
    • POST /api/worker/register – Worker signup

4.2 Optional customer / session APIs
    • POST /api/register – Optional customer account (not on the Get Started path)
    • POST /api/login – Authenticate user / worker / admin
    • GET /api/me – Current authenticated profile
    • GET /api/bookings – Authenticated user’s or worker’s connections
    • POST /api/bookings/{id}/rate – Rate a completed job

4.3 Worker APIs (auth)
    • GET|POST /api/worker/availability – Read or update availability
    • POST /api/worker/update-location – Update live location
    • GET /api/worker/dashboard – Incoming connections
    • PATCH /api/worker/bookings/{id} – Update booking status

4.4 Admin APIs (auth + admin role)
    • GET /api/admin/dashboard
    • GET /api/admin/users
    • GET /api/admin/workers
    • GET /api/admin/bookings
    • POST /api/admin/workers/{id}/approve
    • POST /api/admin/workers/{id}/reject

5. Core Features (MVP)
User Features
    • Open Get Started and see a map immediately (no signup)
    • Choose a service and see nearby workers as map pins
    • Connect instantly with name and phone
    • See the worker’s phone only after connecting
Worker Features
    • Self-registration and profile setup
    • Admin verification before appearing on the public map
    • Update availability status
    • Update live location
    • Receive incoming guest or user connections
Admin Features
    • Dashboard to monitor users, workers, and bookings
    • Verify workers
    • Track connections made (including guest name/phone)

6. Technical Considerations
    1. Maps and Distance
        • Haversine formula to rank workers within a radius (default 20 km)
        • Leaflet for the web map
    2. Privacy
        • Worker phone numbers are not listed on the public nearby API
        • Phone is returned only on a successful POST /api/book
    3. Security
        • Password hashing (bcrypt) for worker and admin accounts
        • HTTPS for secure connections
        • Role-based access (optional user / worker / admin)
    4. Scalability
        • MVP: Host on shared cloud (DigitalOcean, AWS Lightsail)
        • Later: Migrate to AWS or GCP for scaling

7. Deployment and Hosting
    • Domain: sharphand.ng
    • Frontend: Vue.js SPA (Laravel + Vite)
    • Backend: Laravel API
    • Database: MySQL
    • Maps: Leaflet / OpenStreetMap (Google Maps optional later)

8. Future Enhancements
    • Optional customer accounts and saved booking history
    • In-app payments (Stripe / Flutterwave)
    • Worker subscription plans and featured listings
    • Ratings analytics and service history
    • Multi-city expansion
    • Native mobile app (iOS/Android)

Summary:
SharpHand.ng is lightweight and hyper-local. The web MVP lets anyone tap Get Started, pick a service on a map, see nearby workers, and connect with only a name and phone number. Worker and admin accounts remain authenticated. Monetization and customer accounts can be added later.
